  "abs_stop_c": 80.0,
  "board_cap_w": 85.0,
  "cap_consecutive": 3,
  "how": "aifoundry2's own lines in E194's and E200's kits (E190 arm A's on this card) and E208's kit on this card: the board strictly above 85 W on 3 samples in a row (a sample with no board reading starts the count again); the shires' mean die (minshire[0]) at or above 80 C; the hottest-sensor latch (minshire[2]) at or above 80 C once it has risen during the session (a latch already high from before the session does not trip until it rises). E189's 65 W / 70 C lines, which E194's and E200's kits read first for their own programs, are not E209's: MM1-v2 puts E209's top point at 67.2 W and E208 read 71.5-71.9 W on this card",
  "trip": "touches the hosts' --stop-file at once (a running host ends at its next launch boundary, about 0.5 s) and nothing further starts; no process is killed"
